  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "@haibala-aii/dsh-extensions-remotelink",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nHaibala mobile remote control for the [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) web GUI: the desktop mints a one-time QR, the phone pairs and uses the normal responsive web UI.\n\nThis is a fork of [`@linxin666/dsh-remote-web-ui`](https://github.com/zhu1090093659/dsh-web-ui) (BSD-3-Clause). See [NOTICE](NOTICE)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:haibala-aii/dsh-extensions-remotelink\n```\n\nRestart `dsh web` after the add succeeds. This repository ships prebuilt `lib/`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "1. Open the desktop GUI at `http://127.0.0.1:<port>` (the pairing panel is loopback-only).\n2. Settings → Remote: turn the plugin on and save.\n3. Scan the QR (or open the copied link) on the phone. The phone binds and reloads into the normal web UI (the sidebar/details collapse automatically on small screens).\n4. **Stop** revokes every paired device. **Refresh** invalidates the current QR.\n\nThe sidebar chip **正在远程操控** appears only while at least one paired phone is online."
    },
    {
      "section": "Task-complete alerts",
      "text": "When an agent goes idle after running, the desktop GUI and an open phone tab play a short chime and show a system notification (after the browser grants permission). Settings → Remote → **任务完成提醒** toggles this on both sides. Keep the web UI open on the phone; Android Chrome can still banner while the tab is in the background. The notification body is the session title only — never an origin or path."
    },
    {
      "section": "Public access (own domain)",
      "text": "Leave **自动公网隧道** off. Point a reverse proxy or named tunnel at `http://127.0.0.1:<port>`, then set **公网地址** to that origin, for example `https://dsh.example.com`. Save and refresh the QR; pick **公网地址**, not a LAN IP.\n\nAlso trust that host on the connection plugin (`--trusted-host dsh.example.com`, or a profile overlay that concatenates it onto `ctx.webRuntime.trustedHosts`)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Public access (own domain)",
      "text": "A Cloudflare *quick* tunnel hostname changes every run and does not forward SSE; chat then polls. A stable hostname on your own domain avoids that churn."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "BSD-3-Clause. Original copyright zhu1090093659; Haibala modifications 2026."
    }
  ],
